// Locks and meeting points for tasks: `Mutex`, `ReadWriteLock`, `Semaphore`,
// `WaitGroup` and `Once`. A task that has to wait is parked, so its thread
// runs other tasks meanwhile, and a lock may be held across an `await` or
// any other call that waits.
//
// Most shared state needs none of these: an `atomic def` runs one caller at
// a time on its object, an `atomic` field is read and written whole, a
// service runs its `@commit` methods one at a time, and a channel hands a
// value from one task to another. Reach for this module when a lock has to
// span several calls, or when tasks have to wait for each other.
partial module std.sync {}
